(ii) the petitioner will make himself available to the police as and when required in course of investigation;
(iii) the petitioner shall appear on each and every date before the Trial court and failure to do so for two consecutive dates without plausible reason will entail cancellation of his/her bail bond by the Trial court itself;
(iv) the petitioner shall appear before the concerned police station every fortnight for next six months to mark attendance;
(v) the petitioner shall in no way try to induce or promise or threat the witnesses or tamper with the evidences, failing which the State shall be at liberty to take steps for cancellation of the bail bonds;
Patna High Court CR. MISC. No.73029 of 2022(2) dt.20-01-2023 (vi) the petitioner shall desist from committing any criminal offence again failing which the State shall be at liberty to take steps for cancellation of the bail bonds.
 (Rajiv Roy, J)
Prakash Narayan /Ajay Singh U T Arnav vs The State Of Bihar on 20 January, 2023 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/33044651/
